{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug fast path)\n\nConfirmed root cause: `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py:143` calls `TarFile.extractall(extracted)` with neither a `filter=` argument nor a class extraction filter. On CPython 3.12.13, `_get_filter_function(None)` deterministically emits the reported `DeprecationWarning` before extracting anything; `pytest -W error::DeprecationWarning tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py::test_install_from_sdist_preserves_commit` failed at that exact branch. The introducing test commit is 5514923afe.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: installing `tarfile.data_filter` as the process-wide default while leaving the test unchanged made the same warning-as-error reproduction pass (1 passed), ruling out the build backend and provenance round-trip as causes. The generated sdist contains exactly five relative regular files, all mode 0644, with no links or special entries. Applying `data_filter` rejected none and changed only uid/gid/uname/gname to None; the unchanged rebuild and exact `abc1234` provenance assertion passed. Python 3.11/3.12 tarfile documentation explicitly recommends setting `filter` according to needed features and says `filter=\"data\"` prevents the most dangerous extraction issues. Repository prior art uses the same policy in `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:214` and `scripts/mutation_gate.py:519`.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect. The ticket acceptance contract requires the named test to pass with this warning promoted to an error and requires an explicit justified extraction policy. The smallest restoration is test-only `filter=\"data\"`, matching Python 3.14’s safe default; it changes no production archive behavior.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is explicit safe extraction of the self-generated sdist with the exact provenance round-trip unchanged. This extractall call is local to one pytest test and has no callers or consumers that depend on the warning or on ownership restoration. No behavioral dependency blocks repair."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786922382582618001,"uuid":"e64bf086-8902-4ed5-b078-2cbe576676b3"}